{
  "_comment": "Shared vision scenarios. Tokens are in grid units (x from the left, y from the bottom row); walls, lights and samples are map pixels (y from the top). Both packages run every scenario; the backend checks which tokens are sent, the frontend checks the tier at each sample and that a token is seen exactly when it is sent. A token's `light` is the torch it carries, lit at its centre; `visible: false` is a hidden token, which no player is sent. Keep both copies identical. A scenario's `grid` replaces the map's grid type and offset for it; on a hex map a token's x and y are its hex (utils/tokenCentre.ts).",
  "map": {
    "width": 20,
    "height": 20,
    "gridSize": 100,
    "gridType": "square",
    "gridOffsetX": 0,
    "gridOffsetY": 0
  },
  "viewer": "p1",
  "scenarios": [
